	(text_box "10 MHz sine from a GPSDO (0.3 V peak or more), or any 0.5 to 3.3 V square wave to 80 MHz. 50 Ω if the shunt is in.\nAC coupled into a TLV3501 comparator on the ADC's low-noise 3.3 V through 1 kΩ, which holds its input clamps under 10 mA for a ±10 V generator: +IN biased to mid-rail through 10 kΩ, -IN at mid-rail, 6 mV of hysteresis inside, 4.5 ns.\nThe FPGA's PLL locks to it: 10 MHz or more for its jitter specification."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 198.12 0)
		(size 193.04 7.62)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2bd34481-5f19-f3c6-550c-7b631524636e")
	)
	(text_box "Any address or data bit can be swapped for routing: the SDRAM controller does not care which ball is A5. Clocked by an FPGA ODDR at up to 100 MHz, no termination, 3.3 V LVCMOS."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 560.07 180.34 0)
		(size 147.32 5.08)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "68d1e063-8d3e-44e4-25c6-dc1333a65613")
	)
	(text_box "Pmod sockets, 0.9 inch apart on the board edge so a double-width module spans both.\n33 Ω series; Pmod pins 1-4 = IO0-3, 7-10 = IO4-7, 5/11 ground, 6/12 3.3 V\n(pads 1,3,5,7 / 2,4,6,8 / 9,10 / 11,12 in KiCad's odd/even numbering).\nBoth buses are drawn; the labels on the socket end are the same bus members."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 599.44 547.37 0)
		(size 72.39 8.89)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.9 0.9)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9b484f57-0217-2e02-ab80-3a7b5150bdf3")
	)
	(text_box "JTAG header: the same four signals the FT2232H drives (USB sheet).\nTCK pulled down, TMS/TDI/TDO pulled up (Lattice checklist).\nTo use an external programmer here, fit JP501 FTDI OFF (USB sheet) first:\nit holds the FT2232H in reset, so its TXD / TCK output cannot fight.\nThese four local labels and the SDRAM bus members\nare the only labels on this sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 539.75 351.79 0)
		(size 60.96 12.7)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
